    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061113.0411\n\nBEIJING, Nov. 14 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nURGENT: WB projects drastic rise in China's current account surplus\n\n\n\n\nThe World Bank predicted on Tuesday that China's current account will post a surplus of 223 billion U.S. dollars this year, a drastic rise from last year's 160 billion U.S. dollars.\n\nThe figure is expected to take up 8.5 percent of China's gross domestic product, said the Washington-based group in its latest mid-year update on East Asia.",
